Message-ID: <00a3e61ea9067888681deb3d1156c3db7572b191.1791454933.git.stefan@agner.ch>
From: Stefan Agner <stefan@agner.ch>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:22:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix test_math import failure on musl

The 3.13 backport of gh-152563 (8e85d73bd6) compares the return value of
support.linked_to_musl() against a version tuple. On the 3.13 branch
linked_to_musl() still returns a bool, so on musl this evaluates
True < (1, 2, 6) and raises TypeError at class definition time. This
makes test_math (and test_cmath, which imports from it) fail to import,
breaking the PGO profile run.

Restore the pre-3.13.16 condition which skips the test on musl.
---
 Lib/test/test_math.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Lib/test/test_math.py b/Lib/test/test_math.py
index b678420..eac5a1c 100644
--- a/Lib/test/test_math.py
+++ b/Lib/test/test_math.py
@@ -2743,7 +2743,7 @@ class FMATests(unittest.TestCase):
     @unittest.skipIf(
         sys.platform.startswith(("freebsd", "wasi", "netbsd", "emscripten"))
         or (sys.platform == "android" and platform.machine() == "x86_64")
-        or (support.linked_to_musl() and support.linked_to_musl() < (1, 2, 6)),  # gh-131032
+        or support.linked_to_musl(),  # gh-131032
         f"this platform doesn't implement IEE 754-2008 properly")
     def test_fma_zero_result(self):
         nonnegative_finites = [0.0, 1e-300, 2.3, 1e300]
